# AWS S3 File Upload via Terraform

Automated the deployment of an S3 object resource using Terraform to transfer an on-premise file to an existing AWS S3 bucket on the Nautilus DevOps infrastructure.

## Task Overview

- **Objective:** Copy `/tmp/xfusion.txt` to the existing S3 bucket `xfusion-cp-76354121`.
- **Tooling:** Terraform (`aws_s3_object` resource)
- **Working Directory:** `/home/bob/terraform`

---

## Configuration

The following resource block was added to the existing `main.tf` file:

```hcl
resource "aws_s3_object" "xfusion_file" {
  bucket = "xfusion-cp-76354121"
  key    = "xfusion.txt"
  source = "/tmp/xfusion.txt"
}
Execution & Verification
Navigated to the Terraform working directory and applied the configuration:

Bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform apply -auto-approve
Verified the successful upload:

Plaintext
aws_s3_object.xfusion_file: Creating...
aws_s3_object.xfusion_file: Creation complete after 0s [id=xfusion.txt]

Apply complete! Resources: 1 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed.
